{"name":"Purple Pizzazz","hex":"#fe4eda","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"},{"term":"pizzazz","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Flair, vitality, or zest; energy; vigor. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pizzazz"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shades of magenta","blocks":[{"text":"The color magenta has notable tints and shades. These various colors are shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Color_icon_magenta.svg/330px-Color_icon_magenta.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_magenta"},{"title":"Pizzazz","blocks":[{"text":"Pizzazz is the fifth album by American singer Patrice Rushen, released in 1979 on Elektra Records."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/38/Pizzazz_%28Patrice_Rushen_album_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pizzazz"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Line_of_purples.png/500px-Line_of_purples.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Line_of_purples.png/500px-Line_of_purples.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The most saturated magentas that humans are able to perceive lie on the line of purples, which connects violet and red in the chromaticity diagram","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALine_of_purples.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/RGB_combination_on_wall.png/500px-RGB_combination_on_wall.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/RGB_combination_on_wall.png/1280px-RGB_combination_on_wall.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/RGB_combination_on_wall.png/500px-RGB_combination_on_wall.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red, green and blue lights, representing the three basic additive primary colors of the RGB color system, red, green, and blue. Magenta light is composed of equal amounts of red and blue light.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARGB_combination_on_wall.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Purple_African_Vio